    <h1>About Tension</h1>
    <p>Tension is an educational publisher for couples who want more than a vanilla routine. We create intelligent, practical, and erotic relationship education for adults exploring kink, BDSM, D/s, and consensual power dynamics.</p>
    <p>Our purpose is straightforward: help couples find the words, build the trust, and create exciting experiences that bring them closer.</p>
    <h2>About Mr. D</h2>
    <p>Mr. D is Tension’s resident editorial guide: direct, kink-informed, occasionally provocative, and interested in what helps real couples communicate and play better.</p>
    <p>Mr. D is an editorial coaching persona created by Tension—not a human therapist, clinician, or licensed professional. His guidance combines established consent practices, relationship frameworks, community knowledge, research, and extensive editorial development.</p>
    <p>A strong point of view should not require blind trust. Safety-related claims are sourced where evidence exists, uncertainty is stated when research is limited, and material corrections are recorded.</p>
    <h2>What Tension is for</h2>
    <p>Tension helps couples ask better questions, communicate more clearly, and approach exploration with consent, care, and realistic expectations. No article or guide creates consent, diagnoses an experience, or replaces qualified professional support.</p>
    <p>Tension is an educational publisher today. A coaching product may come later; when it does, its technology and limitations will be disclosed clearly.</p>
    <p>Questions or corrections: <a href="mailto:hello@tension.app">hello@tension.app</a>.</p>
  </article>
